 little  bit more general and the website how the  website works very simply you go to the  website you say what your goal is you  say how much money you want to put  towards that goal you say who has the  power to declare you a failure  so usually here this has to be someone  you trust you don't have to have a  referent a lot of people do choose to do  their contracts on their honor but the  trick with the referee is you really  have to trust them not just to report  honestly about you if you succeed but  the trick really is finding a referee  who's willing to actually report you as  a failure right and then you say where  the money goes if you fail and that  money can go to the referee a lot of  people do that other people choose  charity and one of the more favorite  options is to choose  the what we call the anti charity so the  way the anti charity works is you're  given a list of ten politically  polarizing charities so the George Bush  library and the Bill Clinton Library and  then we took four kind of hot social  issues and we took two charities that  work on both sides work on either side  and so your idea is you supposed to  choose what you hate the most and that's  where your money goes if you fail and  have you you stick yourself so stick  very much is a manifestation of my  personal life with respect so actually  starting in graduate school I wrote a  contract with a fellow graduate student  and to lose weight and we lost 40 pounds  we both lost the weight and then we both  had a maintenance contract that went on  for many years and so I am very much a  user of this concept in my own life as  well okay and the address is at

